# Sandbox prompt layering

Do **not** bake operator-specific jobs (Excel SOP, OpenAI SDK, a project's
build steps, etc.) into the builtin Sandbox prompt. That prompt is the
product-level sandbox contract. It already follows this design — do not
“fix” it by assuming tools or packages are installed.

## Layers

| Layer | Where | What belongs there |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Product / builtin tool | `src/tools/sandbox/systemRole.ts` (manifest in `src/tools/sandbox/index.ts`) | `SANDBOX_SHARED_INSTRUCTION` is the General instruction for every sandbox whose base is general: working directory, time limits, `startJob`, file delivery, secret variables and files, and the matplotlib `plot_N.png` fact. It does not name programs a particular image has. Image-specific guidance lives only in that card's extra instruction. `base: none` uses only that profile's text. A saved General instruction (`_shared`) replaces the shared contract for every profile still using it |
| Sandbox Hub profile | Operator `SANDBOX_PROFILES_FILE` → `instruction` (file or text) per profile | A purpose-built sandbox (its own image, network, limits). The composed instruction is that tool's system role, injected only while that profile's tool is on. `base: general` (default) prepends the General instruction (the saved `_shared` row, else `SANDBOX_SHARED_INSTRUCTION`), then that profile's extra text. `base: none` uses only the extra text. The same stored fields always produce the same bytes, so the prefix stays cache-stable. Admins (`SANDBOX_HUB_ADMINS`) edit the General instruction and each profile's extra instruction. Reset on the General instruction restores `SANDBOX_SHARED_INSTRUCTION`. Reset on a card clears that profile's extra text |
| Sandbox image | `docker/opensandbox/` (requirements, apt list, Node.js) | Makes `import`, CLIs, and runtimes available. Rebuild the image and point `OPENSANDBOX_IMAGE` (or a profile's `image`) at it |
| Assistant prompt | Agent Setting → system role | Standing specialty for **that** assistant (e.g. “`openai` is installed; use it for SDK experiments”) |
| User general instruction | Settings | All chats for that account |
| Topic | **No topic system-prompt field** | Title + compaction `historySummary` only. Use a dedicated assistant, a Skill, or the user message |
| Skills | Activated per conversation from the chat input Skills picker (no `load_skill` tool any more) | Reusable task bundle without a ChatHub release |

## Do not

- Change the builtin prompt because one host installed extra packages or CLIs.
  Give that host's image its own Sandbox Hub profile with its own instruction.
- Claim the `packages` argument installs anything.
- Inject ChatHub LLM keys or other server secrets into the sandbox
  (`OPENAI_API_KEY` on the ChatHub container is **not** in the sandbox; a
  network SDK needs a key and egress allowed by the operator). Keys reach a
  sandbox only as Sandbox Hub environment variables or files that an admin
  (shared) or the user (their own) set in the Hub; the prompt names them
  generically and never lists names, paths or values.
- Invent a topic prompt. `topics.metadata` has no instruction field.

## Files vs Knowledge Base

Any **chat attachment** on that topic (not Excel-only) is synced into the
sandbox working directory under size/count caps, once per file id. Knowledge
Base files are MarkItDown/RAG only unless also attached to the message.

User-facing setup:
[Code Interpreter with OpenSandbox](https://github.com/lqdflying/chathub/wiki/Code-Interpreter-with-OpenSandbox).
